## .NET build output
bin/
obj/
obj_verify/
*.user
*.suo

## Locally-produced deployment artifacts (regenerated by scripts/package-agent.ps1 /
## the GitHub Actions release workflow - never hand-authored, never committed).
## The local `publish/` folder (ad-hoc `dotnet publish` output) is likewise generated,
## not deployment metadata that belongs in source control.
publish/
dist/
*.zip
*.sha256

## Installer temp/output files (installer\Output\CloudOrcAgentSetup.exe is a build
## artifact produced by ISCC from installer\CloudOrcAgentSetup.iss - never hand-authored)
*.tmp
installer/Output/
CloudOrcAgent-install-*/
CloudOrcAgent-extract-*/
CloudOrcAgent-bootstrap-*/

## Visual Studio / VS Code / Rider
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.userprefs

## Test results / coverage
TestResults/
*.trx
coverage/
*.coverage
*.coveragexml

## Logs and runtime state (this project always writes these under
## C:\ProgramData\CloudOrc\... on the target machine, never inside the repo - these
## patterns exist only to catch anything accidentally generated in-place during local dev)
*.log
logs/

## Local development configuration overrides / secrets - never commit real values
appsettings.local.json
appsettings.*.local.json
*.env
.env
.env.*

## Credentials, certificates, private keys - never commit
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
*.cer
*.crt
## Narrow, file-convention patterns only - a blanket *credential*/*secrets* previously
## matched (and silently dropped from version control) legitimate source files like
## CredentialStore.cs. Match actual secret-file conventions instead.
*.credentials
credentials.json
*.secrets
secrets.json
appsettings.secrets.json

## User-specific files
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

## OS files
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

## Local AI-assistant tool state (session-local, not project source)
.claude/
